  "term": "geniculate nucleus",
  "definition": "The geniculate nucleus is a part of the diencephalon located below the back end of the dorsal thalamus. It includes a lateral division that passes visual signals to the calcarine cortex and a medial division that passes auditory signals to the auditory cortex.",
